From eb84fa49d3cf1366a268976e57cca24167ed9f2e Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 02:47:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Translate registered menu, shortcut and widget labels at
 render time

Extensions register header menu items, shortcuts, dashboard widgets and
template resource types once, when the console boots and before the
user's locale is applied, so text translated there stays in the boot
locale.

- Add a translate-label helper and util: a value that is a known
  translation key is translated, anything else renders unchanged, so
  extensions can register keys while plain English titles keep working.
- Use it for widget names and descriptions in the widget picker, the
  extension navigation bar, dropdown, customiser and mobile navbar, and
  template builder resource labels; the dropdown and widget picker
  searches match the displayed text.
- Store the English text, not the key, as the name and description of
  widgets added to a dashboard, as before keys were supported.
- Move the extension navigation menu's own text and the widget picker's
  "Added" badge to console translation keys.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01QA1NRoN2Ruts2k2UpHENmQ
